---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Imagine" description="What Grok Imagine is: xAI image and video generation and editing.">
  <section class="about-content">
    <p class="home-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Products</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Imagine</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle muted">Image and video generation and editing in the Grok product line.</p>
    <p><strong>Imagine</strong> is xAI's media generation surface inside Grok. It covers creating and editing images, and related video features when those are announced.</p>
    <p>Where the core <a href="/models">models</a> focus on language and reasoning, Imagine focuses on visual output.</p>
    <h2>Imagine Image</h2>
    <p>Official updates have described successive image models, including <strong>Imagine Image 2.0</strong>, announced with emphasis on precision editing, clearer text in images, improved factuality, and usefulness for real work.</p>
    <h2>Imagine Video</h2>
    <p>xAI has also shipped video-related updates under Imagine, including features such as text-to-video and higher output quality where announced.</p>
    <h2>What Imagine is for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Generating images from text prompts</li>
      <li>Editing and refining generated images</li>
      <li>Video-related generation where those features are available</li>
      <li>Using Imagine through Grok apps and, where offered, API access</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>How Imagine fits the wider stack</h2>
    <p>Imagine is the media layer of the Grok ecosystem, alongside <a href="/voice">Voice</a>, <a href="/bot">Grok Bot</a>, and <a href="/build">Grok Build</a>.</p>
    <h2>How Grokati covers Imagine</h2>
    <p>We publish sourced notes on new image models, editing tools, video features, and API availability when official accounts announce them.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 2rem;"><a href="/products">← All products</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>